WEBVTT

00:11.560 --> 00:16.440
‎Hayato's voice
‎broke the sound barrier again.

00:17.065 --> 00:20.944
<i>‎Yota's been acting strange
‎ever since the sports festival.</i>

00:21.028 --> 00:22.029
‎SPORTS FESTIVAL

00:22.112 --> 00:23.697
<i>‎And he was in such good spirits.</i>

00:23.780 --> 00:25.115
‎SPACING OUT - KARAOKE

00:25.198 --> 00:26.700
<i>‎It's like his mind is elsewhere.</i>

00:26.783 --> 00:28.118
‎SCUTTLING AWAY - THE HALLWAY

00:28.201 --> 00:30.203
<i>‎And Miki seems to be avoiding him too.</i>

00:30.996 --> 00:34.458
<i>‎Did something happen between them
‎that day after school?</i>

00:35.292 --> 00:36.293
‎POKE POKE

00:36.376 --> 00:37.461
‎-Miki.
‎-What?

00:37.544 --> 00:38.587
‎STOP THAT

00:38.670 --> 00:40.213
‎-How you doing?
‎-Huh?

00:40.297 --> 00:41.298
‎CRINGE

00:41.381 --> 00:42.382
‎Why do you ask?

00:42.466 --> 00:43.467
<i>‎She sucks at this.</i>

00:43.550 --> 00:46.845
‎Just so you know,
‎I'm not "not" fine, okay?

00:46.928 --> 00:48.847
‎I'm just a little sleepy.

00:49.556 --> 00:50.474
‎EEK

00:51.975 --> 00:53.852
‎Yeah? Well, that's good then.

00:58.440 --> 01:02.611
<i>‎Miki's been acting strange
‎ever since the sports festival.</i>

01:02.694 --> 01:05.572
<i>‎And she was in such good spirits.</i>

01:06.198 --> 01:07.199
<i>‎What happened?</i>

01:08.825 --> 01:10.911
<i>‎She's making that grim face again.</i>

01:13.246 --> 01:16.541
<i>‎Did something happen with Yota
‎when they were on clean-up duty?</i>

01:18.835 --> 01:19.878
‎Yota.

01:19.961 --> 01:20.962
‎GLIDE

01:21.046 --> 01:22.464
‎Koyun? What's up?

01:23.340 --> 01:24.841
‎Well...

01:25.884 --> 01:27.010
‎How you doing?

01:27.594 --> 01:29.137
‎(TRIES TO) SMILE

01:31.348 --> 01:33.016
‎PFFT - HUH?

01:33.099 --> 01:34.351
<i>‎She sucks at this.</i>

01:35.894 --> 01:37.771
‎Shall we step outside?

01:40.482 --> 01:41.858
‎Miki found out.

01:42.734 --> 01:45.654
‎What? Do you mean...

01:45.737 --> 01:47.739
‎Did you tell her?

01:47.823 --> 01:52.661
‎No, it kind of just slipped
‎based on my behavior.

01:52.744 --> 01:57.040
‎If I'd have just kept it together,
‎she wouldn't have found out.

01:57.124 --> 01:59.751
‎She wasn't giving off any signs
‎that she'd noticed or anything.

02:01.086 --> 02:06.174
‎For a moment, I was actually hoping
‎she'd just get the message already.

02:08.677 --> 02:11.221
‎I said I was fine with the way things are.

02:11.304 --> 02:13.306
‎I really should learn
‎to make my mind up, hey?

02:14.224 --> 02:17.561
‎But Miki already thinks highly of you.

02:18.228 --> 02:21.982
‎If she knows you like her now,
‎she might start to feel the same way.

02:22.607 --> 02:23.942
‎I don't think she will.

02:25.068 --> 02:29.531
‎Miki's only ever seen me as a friend.
‎Ever since middle school.

02:29.614 --> 02:31.324
‎At best, her best friend.

02:32.492 --> 02:34.077
‎I hope I am.

02:35.912 --> 02:41.084
‎And honestly, I'm fine with that.

02:41.168 --> 02:44.754
‎Or at least I thought I was.

02:49.885 --> 02:53.138
‎She knows how you feel about her now,

02:53.221 --> 02:57.350
‎but that doesn't mean she'll suddenly
‎hate you or try to cut ties with you.

02:57.934 --> 03:01.479
‎It must be that she just doesn't know
‎how to handle this right now.

03:01.563 --> 03:04.816
‎Miki cares about the people around her.

03:05.692 --> 03:07.944
‎She won't do anything reckless.

03:10.697 --> 03:11.990
‎You're right.

03:12.073 --> 03:16.536
‎Which is why I don't think I can let
‎things stay as ambiguous as they are.

03:18.872 --> 03:20.749
‎Koyun. I...

03:21.917 --> 03:23.668
‎I'm going to put an end to this.

03:26.504 --> 03:30.926
‎EPISODE 14
‎BOMBSHELL

03:31.551 --> 03:34.721
<i>‎I think Yota likes me...</i>

03:34.804 --> 03:39.351
<i>‎I can't exactly talk to Minato,
‎or anyone, really, about this.</i>

03:39.434 --> 03:41.478
<i>‎Even if it's all in my head,</i>

03:41.561 --> 03:44.022
<i>‎or even if it's all actually real...</i>

03:44.105 --> 03:47.400
<i>‎If I talk to someone about it,
‎that'll just hurt Yota.</i>

03:48.818 --> 03:50.904
<i>‎And what about Koyun?</i>

03:50.987 --> 03:53.782
<i>‎If Koyun likes Yota, then...</i>

03:54.449 --> 03:58.078
<i>‎Then I end up hurting two people!</i>

03:59.162 --> 04:00.455
‎Check, please.

04:00.538 --> 04:02.791
‎Yes! On my way!

04:06.711 --> 04:09.506
‎Yo, Miki.
‎Did something happen at school again?

04:10.298 --> 04:12.676
‎You've had this dreadful look
‎about you all day.

04:12.759 --> 04:15.220
‎You could tell? I'm so sorry.

04:15.303 --> 04:16.721
‎Go on, then.

04:16.805 --> 04:18.348
‎Let's hear your complaints.

04:18.431 --> 04:20.725
‎No, I don't have any complaints.

04:22.394 --> 04:26.606
<i>‎But it might be easier to talk to these
‎guys instead of the people at school.</i>

04:27.983 --> 04:29.109
‎Well...

04:31.111 --> 04:35.782
‎I may have just found out that somebody
‎who I thought was a friend

04:35.865 --> 04:39.369
‎may actually have real feelings for me.

04:39.953 --> 04:41.955
‎What do you think I should do?

04:43.957 --> 04:47.377
‎Should I pretend like I haven't noticed
‎and just go about my life as usual?

04:47.877 --> 04:50.505
‎Or maybe I should avoid them...

04:51.006 --> 04:52.882
‎I don't know what to do.

04:52.966 --> 04:53.967
‎DAMAGE

04:54.050 --> 04:55.635
<i>‎-Young love.
‎-Young love.</i>

04:56.678 --> 05:00.765
‎I'd probably feel flattered,
‎so long as I didn't hate the person.

05:01.933 --> 05:04.686
‎In fact, if I found out a girl liked me,

05:04.769 --> 05:07.981
‎that'd probably prompt me
‎to go on and ask her out myself.

05:08.064 --> 05:09.065
‎Really?

05:09.149 --> 05:11.860
‎But what if things go wrong?

05:11.943 --> 05:14.404
‎Then you've lost a friend
‎in addition to a romantic partner.

05:15.030 --> 05:19.075
‎Yeah, but I still hang out with my exes.
‎We grab food like nothing's happened.

05:19.159 --> 05:21.661
‎Man, I don't think I could do that.

05:21.745 --> 05:25.165
‎As you get older, you get more and more
‎of those fuzzy sorts of relationships.

05:25.248 --> 05:26.416
‎Speak for yourself.

05:27.042 --> 05:29.586
‎Is this friend of yours a boy or a girl?

05:29.669 --> 05:30.879
‎It's a boy.

05:30.962 --> 05:32.797
‎Then I'm not so sure.

05:32.881 --> 05:38.386
‎When it's unrequited love from someone
‎you can't physically beat in a one-to-one,

05:38.470 --> 05:40.889
‎it's best to nip that shit in the bud.

05:40.972 --> 05:45.185
‎Based on my experience in battle with men,
‎you really need to have yourself a weapon.

05:45.268 --> 05:46.686
‎Who hurt you?

05:46.770 --> 05:47.771
‎GROANS

05:47.854 --> 05:52.859
‎A jilted girl and a jilted guy
‎are two very different things.

05:53.485 --> 05:57.572
‎He's not the type to fly into a rage,
‎so I think I'll be fine in that regard.

05:58.406 --> 06:02.952
‎Well, things would be much easier
‎if you ended up with feelings for him too.

06:04.162 --> 06:05.872
<i>‎Feelings for him too...</i>

06:09.834 --> 06:12.462
<i>‎When I'm with Yota...</i>

06:13.046 --> 06:16.424
<i>‎I feel like myself,
‎and we always have a good time.</i>

06:16.508 --> 06:19.803
<i>‎I'm sure Yota feels the same way.</i>

06:20.303 --> 06:23.807
<i>‎We are each
‎a cozy place of warmth for the other.</i>

06:23.890 --> 06:25.475
<i>‎Friends on equal footing.</i>

06:26.559 --> 06:28.895
<i>‎How I wish that were the case...</i>

06:30.438 --> 06:32.857
‎CAMERA ROLL

06:37.946 --> 06:41.199
<i>‎What if I weren't a girl?</i>

06:41.282 --> 06:43.576
<i>‎What if I weren't
‎a potential love interest?</i>

06:44.661 --> 06:47.705
<i>‎Would we have gotten as close as we have?</i>

06:47.789 --> 06:49.707
<i>‎Would he still have treated me
‎just as nice?</i>

06:50.834 --> 06:52.961
<i>‎I want Yota to see me</i>

06:53.962 --> 06:57.048
<i>‎not as a girl, not as a love interest,</i>

06:57.882 --> 07:01.594
<i>‎but as a human being worthy of friendship.</i>

07:07.725 --> 07:08.726
‎INCOMING CALL - NINE AUDIO

07:08.810 --> 07:09.811
‎Minato?

07:11.146 --> 07:12.397
‎Hello?

07:12.480 --> 07:14.816
<i>‎Hello. Are you free to talk?</i>

07:14.899 --> 07:17.152
‎Yeah. Are you out right now?

07:17.235 --> 07:19.737
‎Yeah. I'm on a walk with Ponta.

07:19.821 --> 07:21.489
<i>‎Little Raccoon-sky?</i>

07:21.573 --> 07:23.575
‎I just told you his name's Ponta.

07:23.658 --> 07:24.701
<i>‎What's up?</i>

07:24.784 --> 07:26.119
‎Not much, really.

07:26.619 --> 07:31.166
‎I was just out for a walk
‎when I got this itch to talk to someone.

07:32.292 --> 07:33.626
‎What the heck?

07:33.710 --> 07:36.880
<i>‎Yeah, there's no real meaning
‎behind my call.</i>

07:37.380 --> 07:40.383
<i>‎But sometimes people
‎just get the itch to talk to others.</i>

07:40.467 --> 07:42.051
‎Yeah. Mood.

07:42.135 --> 07:45.263
‎But are you sure
‎you're so itching to talk to me?

07:45.346 --> 07:46.347
<i>‎Why's that?</i>

07:46.431 --> 07:48.600
‎Don't you have girls lining up...

07:48.683 --> 07:49.684
‎MEMORIES OF MIDDLE SCHOOL

07:49.767 --> 07:51.311
‎...to talk to you on the phone?

07:51.394 --> 07:53.021
<i>‎Is that what you think of me?</i>

07:53.646 --> 07:55.607
‎There's no one like that for me.

07:55.690 --> 07:59.569
‎And even if there were, I'd reach out to
‎them with a talking point already in mind.

07:59.652 --> 08:01.070
<i>‎And you wouldn't for me?</i>

08:01.154 --> 08:04.073
‎Why would I?
‎It's not like that between us.

08:06.659 --> 08:09.329
<i>‎What's with the pause?
‎Does this disappoint you?</i>

08:09.412 --> 08:10.788
‎Not at all!

08:10.872 --> 08:12.624
<i>‎I'm sorry I made you sad.</i>

08:12.707 --> 08:13.833
‎Shut up, you!

08:13.917 --> 08:15.084
<i>‎I'm just kidding.</i>

08:15.168 --> 08:17.170
‎Oh, my gosh.

08:17.253 --> 08:19.923
‎I'm out too, and you've got me
‎looking like a weirdo

08:20.006 --> 08:21.925
‎who yells in bicycle parking lots.

08:22.008 --> 08:24.093
<i>‎Are you just on your way home?
‎A little late, no?</i>

08:24.177 --> 08:25.386
‎Yeah. I had work.

08:25.470 --> 08:26.971
‎I'm getting on my bike now.

08:27.055 --> 08:30.183
‎I'm heading home too.
‎Little Pon's tired and won't move.

08:30.266 --> 08:31.851
‎-<i>‎Pon-pooped.</i>
‎-It's just Ponta.

08:31.935 --> 08:33.269
<i>‎Talk to you later.</i>

08:33.353 --> 08:34.687
<i>‎Was I a good killer for time?</i>

08:34.771 --> 08:35.897
‎You were. Thanks.

08:36.397 --> 08:39.359
‎And feel free to call me
‎if you ever feel the need to talk.

08:40.360 --> 08:42.862
‎-I will.
‎-<i>‎See you tomorrow at the wrap party.</i>

08:42.946 --> 08:45.240
‎For the cheer squad! Yakiniku!

08:45.323 --> 08:47.617
<i>‎Had you forgotten?
‎Make sure to come, okay?</i>

08:48.993 --> 08:50.537
‎Yeah. Thanks.

08:50.620 --> 08:51.704
<i>‎Good night.</i>

08:58.127 --> 09:03.466
<i>‎I wonder how Miki actually feels
‎about Yota right now.</i>

09:04.008 --> 09:07.887
<i>‎Does she see him as a friend,
‎like Amamiya?</i>

09:07.971 --> 09:10.223
‎How long have you known Minato?

09:10.306 --> 09:11.599
‎Come with me.

09:11.683 --> 09:14.727
‎Koyun. Are Yota and Minato
‎"different" for you?

09:15.353 --> 09:17.313
<i>‎Does she?</i>

09:17.397 --> 09:18.481
<i>‎Wait...</i>

09:19.148 --> 09:21.442
<i>‎How does Miki see Amamiya,</i>

09:21.526 --> 09:23.778
<i>‎and how does Amamiya see Miki?</i>

09:24.279 --> 09:26.489
<i>‎As friends? Best friends?</i>

09:26.990 --> 09:29.659
<i>‎Or is it something more?</i>

09:30.326 --> 09:34.747
<i>‎I wonder how Amamiya sees me...</i>

09:34.831 --> 09:37.750
<i>‎Wait, who cares about me!</i>

09:38.793 --> 09:42.005
<i>‎Either way,
‎I hope they're both back to normal</i>

09:42.088 --> 09:45.008
<i>‎at the cheer squad wrap party tomorrow.</i>

09:46.342 --> 09:48.136
‎YAKINIKU - ALL YOU CAN EAT
‎MEAT

09:48.219 --> 09:50.096
‎Well done on the sports festival!

09:51.723 --> 09:54.225
‎Hey, Miki. You look good with short hair.

09:54.309 --> 09:56.644
‎Never go with salt. Always marinade.

09:56.728 --> 09:57.979
‎Maybe I should go short too?

09:58.813 --> 10:00.481
<i>‎They're not.</i>

10:01.524 --> 10:06.195
<i>‎Miki normally hangs out
‎with the guys in our grade,</i>

10:06.279 --> 10:08.906
<i>‎but today,
‎she won't stop talking to the seniors.</i>

10:08.990 --> 10:11.200
<i>‎Is it because this is a special occasion?</i>

10:11.993 --> 10:13.411
<i>‎Am I overthinking this?</i>

10:13.995 --> 10:18.041
<i>‎And Yota hasn't even tried to move
‎from where he first sat down.</i>

10:18.124 --> 10:19.500
‎STARE
‎IN NO POSITION TO TALK

10:19.584 --> 10:21.794
‎Koyuki. They're gonna burn.

10:27.383 --> 10:29.761
‎-You are so right.
‎-<i>‎Amamiya.</i>

10:29.844 --> 10:32.597
<i>‎You look kind of cute today.</i>

10:32.680 --> 10:33.806
<i>‎You're wearing glasses.</i>

10:34.932 --> 10:39.562
‎Hey, guys. Don't you think Amamiya
‎and Momoka have similar kind of outfits?

10:39.646 --> 10:40.813
‎-Huh?
‎-Huh?

10:40.897 --> 10:42.607
‎Stand next to each other.

10:42.690 --> 10:43.691
‎HUH?

10:44.359 --> 10:46.861
‎Wow, you look great together!
‎What a cute couple.

10:47.362 --> 10:49.656
‎-Thankies!
‎-You flirt.

10:49.739 --> 10:51.282
‎BARF

10:51.366 --> 10:52.909
‎He's that kind of guy...

10:53.493 --> 10:56.204
‎Wow, this is kind of embarrassing.

10:57.664 --> 11:00.792
‎They'll start teasing you more
‎if you show that you'll get shy.

11:00.875 --> 11:02.919
‎They'll lose interest
‎if you just go along with it.

11:05.713 --> 11:07.006
‎Amamiya...

11:08.007 --> 11:10.343
‎-You sly fox, you.
‎-You think so?

11:10.426 --> 11:11.427
‎PLAYING DUMB

11:17.600 --> 11:18.684
<i>‎Koyun.</i>

11:18.768 --> 11:20.686
‎SILENCE

11:21.396 --> 11:23.314
‎Hey, Koyuki.

11:23.856 --> 11:26.192
‎I've been wondering...

11:26.901 --> 11:30.071
‎Do you not really like Amamiya?

11:31.280 --> 11:33.116
‎What? Why?

11:33.199 --> 11:36.702
‎Well, I mean, it kind of looks that way...

11:36.786 --> 11:39.247
‎No. Not at all. That's not true.

11:39.330 --> 11:40.581
‎Truly. Not at all!

11:41.165 --> 11:43.459
<i>‎That actually makes me suspicious.</i>

11:44.252 --> 11:46.254
‎Is that really the impression I give?

11:46.337 --> 11:49.924
‎Well, you don't "not" give it?

11:50.425 --> 11:52.301
‎I don't want that.

11:52.385 --> 11:53.845
‎I'll have to rethink things.

11:53.928 --> 11:56.431
‎No, there's no need to force the issue.

11:57.849 --> 11:59.308
‎Mind if I sit here?

12:00.017 --> 12:01.310
‎Momoka!

12:01.394 --> 12:05.273
‎Boy, does my face feel hot.
‎I'm so embarrassed.

12:05.356 --> 12:07.191
‎It sucks when they get carried away.

12:07.275 --> 12:08.693
‎It's fine.

12:08.776 --> 12:12.405
‎Because I actually really do like Amamiya.

12:13.739 --> 12:15.908
‎Is it really that much of a surprise?

12:15.992 --> 12:18.786
‎Do you mean as, like, a love interest?

12:18.870 --> 12:20.538
‎Yep. That's right.

12:20.621 --> 12:24.041
‎And so I was really happy
‎when they said we looked great together.

12:24.625 --> 12:26.961
‎How nice...

12:27.044 --> 12:28.796
<i>‎But Amamiya likes...</i>

12:29.380 --> 12:31.549
‎What do you think, Koyun?

12:31.632 --> 12:33.968
‎Huh? What do I think?

12:34.051 --> 12:37.263
‎Do you think I should give it a shot?

12:37.346 --> 12:40.808
‎That's for you to decide.

12:41.517 --> 12:44.437
‎Who am I to tell you what to do?

12:44.520 --> 12:46.022
‎I'm glad to hear that.

12:46.105 --> 12:50.818
‎I thought if you were against it, Koyun,
‎then my hands would be completely tied.

12:52.028 --> 12:53.446
‎Why me?

12:53.529 --> 12:56.657
‎I mean, if the feeling's mutual,

12:56.741 --> 12:59.452
‎there's no way
‎I could compete with you, right?

12:59.535 --> 13:02.079
‎If the feeling's mutual?

13:02.163 --> 13:03.456
‎-With who?
‎-<i>‎Oh, no!</i>

13:03.539 --> 13:06.709
‎Oh, my. Are you playing coy?

13:07.668 --> 13:09.212
<i>‎No, no, no!</i>

13:10.421 --> 13:12.965
‎We all know who Amamiya likes.

13:13.549 --> 13:16.093
‎It's obviously you.

13:18.971 --> 13:20.223
<i>‎It's over...</i>

13:23.142 --> 13:25.686
‎We all know who Amamiya likes.

13:26.270 --> 13:28.814
‎It's obviously you.

13:31.400 --> 13:32.401
‎What?

13:32.902 --> 13:36.948
‎Amamiya likes me?

13:39.242 --> 13:40.326
‎You're faking it.

13:40.409 --> 13:43.329
‎By that reaction?
‎You're clearly faking it.

13:43.913 --> 13:46.582
‎Surely you know, Koyun.

13:46.666 --> 13:48.584
‎You know how Amamiya feels about you.

13:48.668 --> 13:55.091
‎Can you really not tell
‎when someone likes you?

13:56.217 --> 14:00.763
‎Amamiya is just nice to everyone.

14:00.846 --> 14:03.391
‎I'm not special.

14:03.891 --> 14:07.520
<i>‎No. If I'm being honest,
‎there are some things that come to mind.</i>

14:08.104 --> 14:11.524
<i>‎But I have to tell myself I'm not special.</i>

14:11.607 --> 14:13.484
<i>‎It's not just me.</i>

14:13.568 --> 14:15.653
<i>‎He'd do it for anyone.</i>

14:15.736 --> 14:17.363
<i>‎I have to tell myself this.</i>

14:18.114 --> 14:20.866
<i>‎I pretend I don't see it,
‎and I turn the other way...</i>

14:20.950 --> 14:22.034
‎WHAT IF I'M WRONG?
‎WHAT IF I'M NOT?

14:22.118 --> 14:23.619
‎WILL OUR RELATIONSHIP CHANGE?
‎FOR BETTER? FOR WORSE?

14:23.703 --> 14:25.580
<i>‎I run from it to protect myself.</i>

14:25.663 --> 14:27.915
<i>‎Maybe somewhere in the back of my mind</i>

14:28.416 --> 14:31.252
<i>‎I really do ask, "What if"?</i>

14:32.211 --> 14:33.379
<i>‎But...</i>

14:33.462 --> 14:36.799
<i>‎I wish it weren't her
‎who made me realize all this.</i>

14:36.883 --> 14:40.511
‎Glad to hear it.
‎I feel so relieved hearing that from you.

14:41.095 --> 14:44.515
‎I'll do my best
‎to make sure he loves me back.

14:44.599 --> 14:45.600
‎NO COMMENT

14:45.683 --> 14:48.144
<i>‎So scary...</i>

14:48.227 --> 14:49.937
<i>‎Her methods are scary.</i>

14:50.980 --> 14:53.900
‎Those who wanna keep the party rolling,
‎we're moving to the riverbank.

14:53.983 --> 14:55.902
‎-Yay!
‎-Let's see...

14:55.985 --> 14:57.862
‎-Fireworks!
‎-Where are my shoes?

15:01.073 --> 15:02.283
‎Looks like we were neighbors.

15:02.366 --> 15:03.618
‎Yep.

15:05.620 --> 15:08.289
‎Wait... Koyun?

15:11.959 --> 15:13.336
‎And we have the same watch.

15:14.128 --> 15:16.130
‎SEIZING UP - WHOA

15:16.213 --> 15:19.175
<i>‎Oh, no... He's going to get the wrong idea.</i>

15:19.258 --> 15:20.968
<i>‎I have to think of a response...</i>

15:22.345 --> 15:23.346
‎WHISPER

15:23.429 --> 15:25.640
‎It was dirt cheap, wasn't it?

15:29.185 --> 15:32.396
‎It was. But it looks so expensive.

15:32.897 --> 15:34.565
‎I thought the same thing.

15:34.649 --> 15:38.486
‎If you don't say anything,
‎then neither will I. Deal?

15:38.569 --> 15:40.571
‎My glasses were dirt cheap too.

15:41.781 --> 15:42.949
‎I see.

15:43.908 --> 15:44.992
<i>‎What do I do?</i>

15:45.493 --> 15:47.912
‎I won't say anything,
‎or I'll be outed too.

15:49.121 --> 15:51.707
<i>‎This is so much fun.</i>

15:55.503 --> 16:01.926
<i>‎I wish we could stay
‎in this dynamic forever.</i>

16:04.845 --> 16:06.138
‎That was close!

16:06.222 --> 16:08.683
‎I thought I'd lost
‎the key to my shoe locker.

16:08.766 --> 16:10.935
‎Azumi. Stay back.

16:11.018 --> 16:12.979
‎Huh? Hey, why?

16:13.062 --> 16:15.022
‎Are you going
‎to see the fireworks after this?

16:15.106 --> 16:17.817
‎Yeah. And Miki and Tsukiko are going too.

16:17.900 --> 16:19.026
‎That's good to hear.

16:20.194 --> 16:23.364
‎We didn't get to talk much today,
‎seeing as our seats were so far apart.

16:23.447 --> 16:24.949
‎I was hoping you'd come.

16:29.036 --> 16:34.542
<i>‎At this point,
‎it's probably safe to say I'm certain.</i>

16:34.625 --> 16:37.586
<i>‎Wait, what do I do?
‎What do I do, what do I do?</i>

16:37.670 --> 16:38.671
‎TURN

16:38.754 --> 16:40.006
‎Is that so...

16:42.758 --> 16:44.093
‎Koyun! Where are you?

16:44.176 --> 16:45.511
‎BA-BUMP - WHOOSH

16:45.594 --> 16:46.595
‎Here I am!

16:46.679 --> 16:49.598
‎ALL ALONE

16:55.855 --> 16:58.482
‎Hey, you coming down, or what?

16:58.566 --> 17:01.027
‎I'm fine. I'm just watching from up here.

17:01.110 --> 17:03.320
‎Lies! You just can't
‎bring yourself to come down!

17:04.572 --> 17:06.115
‎You can do it. See?

17:06.198 --> 17:07.199
‎LIFT

17:07.283 --> 17:08.451
‎-Here!
‎-Hey!

17:09.618 --> 17:10.828
‎I'm scared! Put me down!

17:10.911 --> 17:12.371
‎Yes, yes. Hold on a sec.

17:15.958 --> 17:17.418
<i>‎Was that a scream?</i>

17:18.002 --> 17:19.253
‎Yo!

17:20.129 --> 17:22.882
‎Koyun and Yota and Tsukko!

17:22.965 --> 17:25.551
‎Yuki. Did you hear a weird voice just now?

17:25.634 --> 17:26.635
‎Oh, that?

17:26.719 --> 17:28.429
‎I was looking out for Atagawa.

17:28.512 --> 17:30.639
<i>‎She looks really angry.</i>

17:31.223 --> 17:35.144
‎Isn't it a little early for sparklers?
‎Aren't they normally saved for last?

17:35.227 --> 17:36.228
‎HMPH

17:36.312 --> 17:38.147
‎It's always a good time for sparklers.

17:38.230 --> 17:39.523
‎Well, this is true.

17:39.607 --> 17:40.733
‎Wanna join us?

17:40.816 --> 17:42.151
‎Don't mind if I do!

17:48.240 --> 17:49.492
‎STARE - RIGHT IN THE MIDDLE

17:49.575 --> 17:51.285
<i>‎Why am I positioned here?</i>

17:51.368 --> 17:53.746
<i>‎Feels like I'm being watched.</i>

17:53.829 --> 17:54.914
‎There goes mine.

17:54.997 --> 17:56.499
‎You're going down with me, Koyun.

17:56.582 --> 17:57.583
‎BLOW

17:57.666 --> 17:58.667
‎Stop that.

18:08.260 --> 18:10.179
‎Mind if I join?

18:14.016 --> 18:15.017
‎Can I sit here?

18:15.101 --> 18:16.102
‎FLINCH

18:16.185 --> 18:17.520
‎Did I do something wrong?

18:22.525 --> 18:24.944
‎THUMP THUMP THUMP

18:25.528 --> 18:27.071
‎-<i>‎This is hilarious.</i>
‎-<i>‎This is hilarious.</i>

18:27.154 --> 18:28.823
‎What kind of faces are those?

18:29.406 --> 18:31.826
‎CRACKLE CRACKLE
‎BANG

18:32.910 --> 18:35.329
‎-Wow!
‎-So cool!

18:36.372 --> 18:37.581
‎Amazing!

18:46.423 --> 18:49.051
‎Shall we see whose can last the longest?

18:49.135 --> 18:50.219
‎Sure.

18:51.011 --> 18:53.055
<i>‎Our elbows are so close.</i>

18:54.557 --> 18:55.558
‎Mine's lit.

19:02.648 --> 19:03.649
<i>‎Smile.</i>

19:03.732 --> 19:04.733
‎SMILE

19:04.817 --> 19:07.236
‎SEIZING UP

19:12.241 --> 19:15.161
‎Cheers to a job well done!

19:15.244 --> 19:16.745
‎-Cheers!
‎-Cheers!

19:21.167 --> 19:22.168
‎Miki.

19:23.419 --> 19:26.255
‎This is yours, isn't it?
‎I found it on the ground.

19:27.590 --> 19:30.384
‎Wait, what? That's my key chain.

19:30.885 --> 19:33.012
‎Hey, you're right.
‎It's not attached to my keys.

19:33.095 --> 19:34.096
‎Here.

19:34.180 --> 19:35.306
‎Thank you.

19:35.389 --> 19:37.516
‎Good on you for knowing it was mine.

19:37.600 --> 19:40.144
‎Of course I'd know it's yours.

19:43.355 --> 19:45.900
‎Hey, Miki.
‎Do you feel awkward being around me?

19:45.983 --> 19:46.984
‎What?

19:47.484 --> 19:49.153
‎You're such an open book.

19:49.737 --> 19:52.740
‎No... I don't feel awkward...

19:53.240 --> 19:54.658
‎I'm sorry.

19:55.451 --> 19:57.661
‎Are you free for a little after this?

20:00.497 --> 20:02.416
‎There's something I need to tell you.

20:18.766 --> 20:19.767
‎Miki.

20:20.267 --> 20:23.270
<i>‎If only he weren't about to say
‎what he's going to say.</i>

20:23.354 --> 20:25.147
<i>‎Then things could stay the same.</i>

20:28.692 --> 20:30.194
‎I like you.

20:30.277 --> 20:31.362
‎What?

20:31.904 --> 20:34.198
‎Well, shucks. Thanks.

20:39.620 --> 20:42.206
<i>‎He's dead serious.</i>

20:43.457 --> 20:46.085
<i>‎That wasn't a joke,
‎and it wasn't flippant.</i>

20:46.168 --> 20:47.962
<i>‎He's being serious.</i>

20:48.879 --> 20:52.800
‎I've liked you all along.
‎Ever since middle school.

20:53.300 --> 20:54.426
‎What?

20:54.510 --> 20:57.346
<i>‎All this time? He's liked me?</i>

20:57.930 --> 21:00.891
‎I never planned on telling you.

21:01.475 --> 21:03.560
‎But I couldn't hide it any longer,

21:04.144 --> 21:05.938
‎and so I wanted to bring it to a head.

21:07.064 --> 21:08.732
‎I want to put an end to this

21:09.400 --> 21:12.611
‎and go back to being just friends.

21:13.487 --> 21:15.614
‎I'm sorry to put you out like this.

21:17.032 --> 21:19.201
<i>‎He's usually so smiley and kind.</i>

21:19.285 --> 21:21.620
<i>‎I've never seen him make this face before.</i>

21:22.538 --> 21:26.208
<i>‎How could I make him
‎make a face like that?</i>

21:27.209 --> 21:29.545
<i>‎I like him too.</i>

21:30.379 --> 21:31.797
<i>‎I love him.</i>

21:32.339 --> 21:33.507
<i>‎But it's not...</i>

21:34.591 --> 21:35.759
<i>‎No.</i>

21:35.843 --> 21:40.556
<i>‎What if I make a conscious effort?
‎Then I might see him in the same way.</i>

21:41.765 --> 21:47.730
<i>‎Who else is going to love me
‎and accept me for who I really am?</i>

21:48.605 --> 21:52.693
<i>‎If I can fall in love with someone
‎in the same way that they love me...</i>

21:54.611 --> 21:57.031
<i>‎Won't that make me happy?</i>

21:58.490 --> 21:59.491
‎Yota.

21:59.992 --> 22:01.285
<i>‎But...</i>

22:05.372 --> 22:06.707
‎I'm sorry.

22:06.790 --> 22:09.543
<i>‎I just can't say yes...</i>

22:09.626 --> 22:12.546
‎It's not that I don't like you too...

22:12.629 --> 22:14.048
<i>‎...while my heart is so unsure.</i>

22:14.131 --> 22:17.843
‎I've just never
‎thought of you in that way.

22:18.969 --> 22:19.970
‎Okay.

22:21.764 --> 22:24.016
‎I don't know what to do.

22:24.850 --> 22:26.602
‎Yeah. I know.

22:28.562 --> 22:31.565
‎I'm sorry I've been avoiding you recently.

22:32.357 --> 22:34.693
‎I didn't mean to hurt you.

22:36.737 --> 22:38.864
‎It's okay. I know.

22:40.657 --> 22:41.867
‎I'm sorry.

22:41.950 --> 22:42.993
‎It's fine.

22:45.037 --> 22:46.038
‎Thank you.

22:51.877 --> 22:53.796
‎Why are you crying?

23:40.968 --> 23:45.973
‎Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
